From 8d357a894f7ed8af024ccd24f292cec920a86045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:53:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: dictionary keys follow a per-key three-way merge (review
 pass 2)

The lockstep-stop resolver judged conflict hunks without the base: a key upstream
had not touched lost our retranslation, and two Malay keys kept the old English
where upstream had translated. Every key of the 24 translated dictionaries is now
ours where only we changed it, upstream's where only upstream did, and rule D4
where both did. Report in the merge notes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/MS.dict | 8 ++++----
 release/src/router/www/RO.dict | 2 +-
 release/src/router/www/RU.dict | 2 +-
 release/src/router/www/SL.dict | 2 +-
 4 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

